nss-clients: release replaced mirred device reference

A non-bind action replace at an explicit index installs the new device with
dev_hold(), but the old act->tcfm_dev reference was overwritten without a
matching dev_put(). Hold the new device, publish it under RTNL, then drop
the old reference.

This closes only the device-reference leak in the replace path. Firmware
mapping replacement, idempotency and the full S05/S06 transaction remain
separate contracts.

--- a/nss_qdisc/igs/nss_mirred.c
+++ b/nss_qdisc/igs/nss_mirred.c
@@ -287,9 +287,16 @@
 	act->tcf_action = parm->action;
 	act->tcfm_from_ifindex = parm->from_ifindex;
 	act->tcfm_to_ifindex = parm->to_ifindex;
-	dev_hold(to_dev);
-	rcu_assign_pointer(act->tcfm_dev, to_dev);
+	{
+		struct net_device *old_dev = rcu_dereference_protected(act->tcfm_dev, 1);
 
+		dev_hold(to_dev);
+		rcu_assign_pointer(act->tcfm_dev, to_dev);
+		if (old_dev) {
+			dev_put(old_dev);
+		}
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * Add the new action instance to the nss mirred action list.
 	 * An existing action (tc replace path) is already linked.
